============================================================
15. FLOAT vs DOUBLE WITH printf()
============================================================

Important concept:

For printf(), a float argument is promoted to double because
of the default argument promotions.

Therefore:

    printf("%f", float_variable);

is correct.

For scanf(), however:

    float  → %f
    double → %lf

This difference is VERY important.


============================================================
16. RETURN VALUE OF printf()
============================================================

printf() returns the number of characters transmitted,
excluding the terminating null character.

Example:

    int n;

    n = printf("Hello");

Typically:

    n = 5


This can occasionally be useful in advanced programming.


